{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>All fat to YHWH, an everlasting statute.</b> In the time of the eternal Temple — the fat of the entrails is forbidden." "<b>For your generations.</b> Even at a time when it is not offered. Lest you say: in the land of Israel it is forbidden but not for all generations — Scripture says <b>for your generations, in all your dwellings</b> — even outside the land." "<b>All fat.</b> Everywhere that sacrifices are mentioned, He warns after it about fat and blood — lest it arise in your heart: since the altar consumes it, I too may [do so]. Scripture says <b>you shall not eat</b> — but for your benefit it is permitted."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:53.552804394Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}